      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and a single dose is usually 1,000 mg or less.\n- This is twice the daily maximum. It would raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release. It may be what you meant, since 1700 could be a typo for 850.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO twice daily with meals**, if the patient is starting metformin. The usual start is 500 mg once or twice daily, increased gradually.\n\nPlease confirm the dose and frequency you want, and check it with your resident or attending. Once you confirm, I'll enter it right away."
      }
